Description: Implements a comprehensive Bayesian dynamic borrowing approach 
    which calibrates both baseline and outcome differences to quantitatively 
    determine the amount of information to borrow from external data. The 
    package uses the propensity score integrated power prior approach to 
    address baseline differences between external and clinical trial subjects 
    and utilizes the elastic prior method to adjust for outcome differences. 
    For adjustment of outcome differences, a class of arctangent elastic 
    functions for the predictive probability of observing the current data 
    given the external data is constructed, which can be easily adapted to 
    clinical input. Methods are available for both continuous and binary 
    outcome scenarios. For methodological details, see Wang et al. (2019) 
    <doi:10.1080/10543406.2019.1657133> for the propensity score integrated 
    power prior and Jiang et al. (2023) <doi:10.1111/biom.13551> for the 
    elastic prior.
